  "traps": ["BNNSVectorDatabase.swift is Tier 2 in Docs/RepoOS/03_FORBIDDEN_EDIT_BOUNDARIES.md: a format change invalidates every user's index.", "Since 5.7 the store does not hold passage text after a load: readableChunks() and allChunks() decode every passage (0.4 s for 144,247 on the Mac) and then keep them until memory pressure. Ask for records, one document or ids when that is all that is needed.", "allChunks() is all or an error: sync pairs it with the vectors by position. Every other reader of text calls readableChunks(), which leaves out a passage whose bytes do not decode. Do not make allChunks() tolerant.", "A load never writes or removes a file. Sync opens a second store on the same files while the app's store may be saving.", "A delete or an update saves anything unsaved before it rewrites the vectors file. The loader relies on it: a cut-off save leaves more vectors than the metadata lists, a cut-off delete leaves fewer, and the same number in another order would load mispaired.", "Positions in passageRecords() are only good until the store changes. Pick from the records, then read by id (chunks(withIDs:), getEmbeddings(forChunkIDs:)).", "Passages come back without vectors (embedding: []). Code that ranks or compares by chunk.embedding gets zeros; ask the store for vectors by id.", "interruptMetadataWrites exists only in debug builds and is for BNNSVectorDatabasePersistenceTests."],
